      "Diary Note": "**Some Thoughts **\n2025-11-20, Thursday, 20:59-21:52\n\nStaring right at someone for too long in VR makes my eyes so dry. Others and I got onto the topic of how you can still feel totally lonely even in a massive crowd. Theo mentioned he mostly comes to these VR events just to hear human voices around him, even if he doesn't say a single word the whole time. Wow, ok. It's true, isn't it? Like, being a quiet observer in a loud digital room is all it takes to heal a bad day. In real life, we can't really stand that close to a stranger or eavesdrop on other people's conversations. Is it simply human nature to peek into other people's lives? And has VR somehow made that socially acceptable?",
