      "Diary Note": "**Some Reflection**\n2026-01-16, Friday, 21:07-21:50\n\nAfter spending time in Social VR, I seem to have become much more of a listener. In VR, if you want to join a conversation, you usually have to listen first before chiming in with your own thoughts, they don't encourage barging in with your own ideas from the get-go. \n\nOn another note, an offline friend mentioned that my jokes can come off a bit sudden sometimes. I never mean to offend anyone, but I guess because no one really knows me in VR, I tend to blurt out jokes without overthinking them. That's definitely something I need to keep in mind. \n\nMoreover, it feels like my overall screen time on other devices has gone down. Since I have to dedicate a chunk of time to my headset every day, I get a bit of digital fatigue. I’ll write more if anything else comes to mind, haha!",
