      "Diary Note": "**Intercultural Communication**\n2026-03-27, Friday, 21:37-22:57\n\nTonight, I was matched with a Japanese player. Upon hearing their hesitant English greeting, I recognized their potential lack of fluency, just as my Japanese was limited to a few basic words. I anticipated that this awkward linguistic barrier would quickly lead to silence.\n\nHowever, they engaged in avatar-mediated communication with me using body gestures, a mix of English and Japanese, and the universally understood \"nodding.\" I responded with an exaggerated gesture of exclamation using both hands.\n\nI viscerally experienced a process of \"Cultural Negotiation.\" It became evident that within the social VR environment, avataric symbols and embodied actions are sufficient to foster genuine connection and resonance between individuals from diverse cultural backgrounds.\n\nFinally, we laughed and waved goodbye to each other, we used the language each had taught the other.",
      "Diary Note (Chinese)": "**跨文化交流**\n2026-03-27, 星期五, 21:37-22:57 \n\n今晚匹配到的是一位日本玩家。听到对方用带点犹豫的英文打招呼时，我知道他的英文可能不太流利，而我的日文也仅限于几个基础单字。感觉这种尴尬的语言壁垒会很快会让空气陷入静默。\n\n但他用肢体手势，在英文、日文以及全人类通用的“频繁点头”之和我进行化身交流。我用双手比出一个夸张的惊叹手势。\n\n我切身感受到了一种“跨文化协商”（Cultural Negotiation）。原来在社交 VR 的世界里，那些化身符号，身体动作，足以让两个来自不同文化背景的人产生真实的联结与共鸣。\n\n最后，我们互相笑着挥手告别。用了对方教的对方的语言",
