      "Diary Note": "**The Paralysis of Infinite Choice**\n2026-07-13, Monday, 20:09-21:04\n\nI stood in my Home Mirror Room in Sir Charletagne for an hour, staring at my massive list of worlds, completely unable to decide where to go. The sheer volume of thousands of accessible spaces triggered a deep decision paralysis. I realized that infinite digital choice can be exhausting. Sometimes, the friction of physical travel is useful because it limits our options and forces commitment to a single location.",
